he Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/illinois/cook-county"],["ARC or PLC in Cook County","/arc-plc/illinois/cook-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 13 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 52% of normal in January to February and 58% in April to May. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 174% and June to July at 151%. Grid 26269 had its driest year in 1956 at 62%.</p>"}
